{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5jyP2uaigY4HUztB1RV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:9-27` — defines Shipment and ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` — in-memory store with save(), findById(), existsById()\n- `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` — REST endpoints (POST /shipments, GET /shipments/{id}, GET /shipments)\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — exception hierarchy with ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum defining machine-readable codes\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — test patterns using MockMvc with jsonPath assertions\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Errors thrown as ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler transforms to JSON envelope\n- Conflict/state errors use `ConflictException(ErrorCode.X, message)` → 409\n- Not-found errors use `ResourceNotFoundException(ErrorCode.Y, message)` → 404\n- Create endpoints return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body()`\n- Tests use `@SpringBootTest`, `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, MockMvc with jsonPath verification\n- Error codes go in `ApiError.kt:31-37` enum and are part of public API\n\n**Affected files:**\n- `ApiError.kt` — must add SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED error code (confirming CANCELLED shipment)\n- `ShipmentController.kt` — must add confirm() endpoint with POST /{shipmentId}/confirm\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for all four cases\n\n**Risks:**\n- Confirm endpoint must be idempotent (CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED succeeds, no change)\n- Operations will retry this call; if retry fails, they lose their ability to track shipments\n- Wrong error code or status breaks error envelope consistency\n\n**Open questions:** None; requirement defines all four cases clearly.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to ErrorCode enum for 409 when trying to confirm a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add endpoint:\n   ```\n   POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm\n   ```\n   Logic:\n   - Get shipment by id; if null, throw ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED (409)\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED and save\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, leave unchanged (idempotent)\n   - Return ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) with the current/updated state\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four tests:\n   - `confirms a created shipment` — POST /shipments/S-1/confirm on CREATED shipment, expect 200 with CONFIRMED status\n   - `confirm on already confirmed succeeds` — POST /shipments/S-1/confirm twice, both succeed\n   - `confirm on cancelled fails` — Create CANCELLED shipment in repository directly, POST confirm, expect 409\n   - `confirm on missing shipment fails` — POST /shipments/nonexistent/confirm, expect 404\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- I considered adding confirm logic to a service layer, but there's no service layer; repository is used directly in controller. Adding service would be unnecessary abstraction for simple state transition.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Logic | Output | Status |\n|------|-------|-------|--------|--------|\n| CREATED→CONFIRMED | shipmentId | Find shipment, validate not CANCELLED, update status, save, return | Shipment with CONFIRMED | 200 |\n| CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED | shipmentId | Find shipment, validate not CANCELLED, no change, return | Shipment with CONFIRMED | 200 |\n| CANCELLED confirm | shipmentId | Find shipment, throw ConflictException | ApiError with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED | 409 |\n| Non-existent confirm | shipmentId | Find null, throw ResourceNotFoundException | ApiError with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND | 404 |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. Test CREATED→CONFIRMED: POST create, then POST confirm, verify status changed in response and persisted\n2. Test idempotency: POST create, POST confirm twice, both return 200 and CONFIRMED, no error\n3. Test CANCELLED rejection: save CANCELLED shipment directly to repo, POST confirm, expect 409 with error code\n4. Test 404: POST confirm on non-existent id, expect 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Starting with adding the error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1948,"cache_read_input_tokens":15291,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1948},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb682ded-bf16-446b-a70b-9cae035978ea","uuid":"dd01ecfc-3951-42e1-a65c-31449d538f9d","timestamp":"2026-09-15T19:01:37.260Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5jyNasD2B4uhSEhJNSD"}
